DECISION
    AUTHOR = Mente / Codex, sob pedido da Founder
    AUTHORITY = Founder, 2026-10-21
    PINKER = linguagem estática que continua sua campanha
    NEXT = linguagem dinâmica implementada em Pinker
    LANGUAGE_IMPLEMENTATION = ainda não iniciada
    CODE_MIGRATION_FROM_V0 = não é a estratégia padrão para o núcleo Next
    MERGE = Founder

BOOTSTRAP
    B0 = compilador Pinker existente e executável no host
    B1 = fontes .pink que implementam a Next
    B2 = executar B1 com Pinker ou construir seu executável nativo no alvo suportado
    B3 = B1 processa e executa programas escritos na linguagem Next
    bootstrap cannot require Next to exist before B1
    compiler Pinker written in Pinker = not required
    Next written in Next = not required or claimed
    native B1 executable != native compilation of B3 programs
    record compiler commit, build mode, runtime/ABI, host tools and commands
    baseline selection = evidence from real bootstrap, not a copied version label

DYNAMIC_CONTRACT_REQUIRED
    values and runtime representation
    arithmetic/ranges/overflow and explicit or implicit conversions
    equality and condition semantics
    scopes, binding/rebinding and calls/returns
    collections and memory ownership/lifetime/reclamation
    runtime type errors with original source location
    input/output and host effects
    syntax and its relation to the Pinker #631 direction
    implementation choices must be explicit before the affected feature is delivered

EVIDENCE_FIRST_SLICE
    choose a small complete set of useful Next programs and expected failures
    map only needed Pinker facilities: text/input, tagged values, collections, calls and resources
    matrix = Next obligation / Pinker source / minimal check / actual gap / bounded repair
    do not assume all facilities exist from documentation alone
    do not add Pinker features solely for hypothetical future Next use
    deliver parsing + real representation + execution + diagnostics + examples + instructions
    expose implemented educational stages, not fabricated intermediate output
    validate every execution mode claimed; honor required native parity
    prototype/stub = investigation evidence only, not completed feature

EDUCATIONAL_HORIZON
    objective = own path inspired by Nand2Tetris, using both Pinkers
    progression = logic/circuits -> architecture -> assembly -> VM -> languages -> system
    proposed Pinker role = typed system/tool components and Next implementation
    proposed Next role = dynamic experimentation and programs in the educational environment
    each stage = representation, invariant, runnable artifact and observable evidence
    simulator/ISA/VM/OS design = not selected here
    SO or bare-metal support = not implemented by this decision

FUTURE_SO
    Founder vision = recreate/host an implementation of Next inside the future system
    current Pinker native target = Linux x86-64 SysV, not proof of portability to that SO
    identify boot, ABI, memory, I/O and runtime services when a port becomes concrete
    separate Next semantics from host services to assess reuse before rewriting
    no immediate kernel, driver, hardware simulator or self-hosting campaign

ORDER
    continue Pinker campaign #768; #631 proceeds according to its authority
    new Next direction does not reorder pending Pinker Tasks automatically
    record bounded Tasks only when there is a concrete independent deliverable
    no requirement to close all historical debts before every useful language delivery
